%% big-endian integer value of one field's ASCII bytes with its separator,
%% written in hex so each byte pair reads as a character code:
%% 16#4D6F6E2C20 is "Mon, ". gnomon:date/0 assembles its 29-byte binary
%% from five of them as fixed-width integer segments.
%%
%% The two combined tables are indexed by the packed value's own bits, so a
%% lookup is a shift and a mask with no multiply; slots no date uses hold 0.
%%
%%   WDAYS_INT        7 entries of 40 bits, Monday first, index weekday + 1
%%   DAYMONTHS_INT  512 entries of 56 bits, "DD Mon ", index month:day bits + 1
%%   YEARS_INT      200 entries of 40 bits, 2000-2199, index year - 1999
%%   HOURMINS_INT  2048 entries of 48 bits, "HH:MM:", index hour:minute bits + 1
%%   SECONDS_INT     60 entries of 48 bits, "SS GMT", index second + 1

